@baseUrl = {{INGESTION_BASE_URL}}

# Run Admin.http first.
#
# What this file verifies:
# 1. Ingestion accepts an authenticated event write, addressed by Source id.
# 2. The event is stored durably and can be fetched back by ID.
# 3. Worker will later fan out the event to matching subscriptions and deliver it
#    to WireMock.
#
# Setup:
# - copy the token from Admin.http createTenantApiKey into src/Integrios.Ingestion/.env
# - copy the id from Admin.http createSource into src/Integrios.Ingestion/.env
# - for the auth-enabled destination path, provision the default file-backed Worker secret at:
#   secrets/acme-corp/erp_api_key (exact secret value; no automatic trimming)
@tenantApiKeyToken = {{$dotenv INGESTION_TENANT_API_KEY}}
@sourceId = {{$dotenv INGESTION_SOURCE_ID}}

###
# Step 1 - Ingest an event
# source_id (query parameter) names the Source created in Admin.http; it resolves to one Topic
# (payments) and one source_contract (event_json). With no mapping configured on the Source, the
# request body below is the Source's output directly: event_type and payload are required,
# source_event_id and metadata are optional. source_event_id becomes part of the idempotency key
# ("{source_id}:{source_event_id}") -- there is no separate idempotency_key field.
# @name ingest
POST {{baseUrl}}/events?source_id={{sourceId}}
Authorization: TenantApiKey {{tenantApiKeyToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event_type": "payment.created",
  "source_event_id": "event_src_001",
  "payload": {
    "paymentId": "pay_001",
    "amount": 1200
  },
  "metadata": {
    "source": "manual-test"
  }
}

###
@eventId = {{ingest.response.body.$.event_id}}

###
# Step 2 - Fetch the accepted event
# This confirms the durable acceptance boundary: Ingestion committed the event
# before async delivery begins.
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}
Authorization: TenantApiKey {{tenantApiKeyToken}}

# Replay is an Admin operation scoped to one dead-lettered EventDelivery, not an Ingestion
# endpoint -- there is no POST /events/{id}/replay here. It requires the OperatorKey and the
# specific delivery id from GET /admin/tenants/{tenantId}/events/{eventId}/deliveries. See the
# full retry/dead-letter/replay walkthrough in docs/setup.md.
